  "notes": [
    "fallback = torch.linalg.matrix_sqrth(A.cpu()).to('mps'); it matches the dispatcher's PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK route within run-to-run noise",
    "timings are medians over synchronized iterations after three warmup calls; this machine runs other probes concurrently, so treat differences under ~20% as noise; loadavg is recorded and min_ms is the cleaner estimate under contention",
    "single matrices and small batches go through eigh's internal CPU branch; there the overlay is slower than the manual fallback (about 0.2x for tiny matrices, 0.8-0.9x at n=256-512) because it adds Python/dispatch work around a route that already copies to the CPU; the batched Metal rows are where it wins (1.4-2.3x)",
    "accuracy is against the CPU kernel on the same input; metal rows inherit eigh's 1e-6 Jacobi tolerance (forward 2e-6..1e-5, gradient 3e-6..5e-5), the cpu_fallback rows match to ~1e-7"
  ]
